{
  "id": 94655763,
  "iid": 2626,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ftype-protocol: Fix crash when comparing _ws.expert to literals",
  "description": "The ftype-protocol has two components to its value - a tvb, which is\nallowed to be be NULL (most notably in _ws.expert), and a string\ndescription. They can also be created from string literals, such as\nin display filters. It's possible to compare protocols with a NULL\ntvb with protocol terms created from literals, e.g. entering the\ndisplay filter \"_ws_expert < 1\".\n\nPartially revert 69e2603c48d04a675785d9e7bad162ebb9a83b07 so that\nthis doesn't crash, by assigning proto_string to the empty string\ninstead of null when creating from a literal. Fixes #17316",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-04-05T13:11:26.323Z",
  "updated_at": "2021-05-24T22:52:44.113Z",
