    {
      "id": "3300ad441f03c0ae2a7afdb27d78cf109688137d",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 545126838,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There are two other spots where `proto_string` is set to `NULL`.  \nShould those also be set to an empty string for consistency?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-04-05T20:01:14.376Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-04-05T20:58:52.616Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 94655763,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2021-05-24T22:36:41.515Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 2626,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 545161360,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The two places you mean are in [line 27](epan/ftypes/ftype-protocol.c#L27) and [line 85](epan/ftypes/ftype-protocol.c#L85)?\n\nLine 85 doesn't really matter, it's the same as how the tvb gets set to NULL in line 84, in that they both get replaced by a real value later either in `val_from_unparsed` or `val_from_string`.\n\nFor line 27 in `value_new()`, it's no different from the string value getting set to NULL in [ftype-string](epan/ftypes/ftype-string.c#L22), it's what happens at a new allocation if an objection is in the NULL equivalence class. The string ftype has the same issues, it's just a dissector bug to do comparisons on NULL objects.\n\nThe issue here is that we have some objects that are not in the NULL equivalence class because either the tvb or the proto_string is non-NULL (but the other is), so they can be compared with normal objects that have both non-null, but not with each other. I think it's consistent with the rest of the code and the other types to allow `value_new()` to return a completely NULL object that shouldn't be used for comparison.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-04-05T20:58:52.567Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-04-05T20:58:52.567Z",
          "system": false,
